<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2">
  <Document>
    <name>🌧️ LIVE PRECIPITATION</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<p><b>Legend</b><br><img src="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/precipitation_na/legend.png" width="600" alt="legend"><br>Precipitation type + intensity (OBSERVED radar echo; 5-75 dBZ severity). <b>Rain</b> ramp: dark green (light) &rarr; green &rarr; yellow &rarr; orange &rarr; red &rarr; magenta &rarr; purple (extreme). <b>Snow/Sleet</b> ramp: pale blue (light) &rarr; blue &rarr; purple (heavy). Same intensity sits at the same position on both ramps. Type is observed/analysed, never inferred from color: MRMS PrecipFlag (snow class 3) inside CONUS and the regional AK/HI/CARIB domains, ECCC SfcPrecipType (snow classes) in Canada, and GFS CSNOW/CICEP for model snow/ice in verified radar gaps only. Echoes from sources that publish no type (OPERA EU, JMA) stay on the Rain ramp. No echo = transparent; GFS pixels are model estimates, never radar. GFS model estimates (not radar) use the same two ramps where no radar covers.</p><p>This entry auto-refreshes from the live overlay (source: NOAA/NSSL MRMS SeamlessHSR hybrid-scan reflectivity composite (CONUS, Alaska, Hawaii, Caribbean; dBZ, public domain) + ECCC North American Radar Composite 1km rain (RADAR_1KM_RRAI, mm/h) / snow (RADAR_1KM_RSNO, cm/h) / precipitation type (Radar_1km_SfcPrecipType) + EUMETNET OPERA EU DBZH composite (CC BY 4.0) in remaining radar gaps + JMA Japan nowcast (attribution) in Japan gaps + NOAA GFS model estimates, same colors (public domain) in verified radar gaps only).</p><p>Turn on/off independently of all other layers. Add this file once; new source cycles appear automatically.</p><p><i>Not endorsed by NOAA.</i></p>]]></description>
    <NetworkLink>
      <name>🌧️ LIVE PRECIPITATION — auto-refresh</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<p><b>Legend</b><br><img src="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/precipitation_na/legend.png" width="600" alt="legend"><br>Precipitation type + intensity (OBSERVED radar echo; 5-75 dBZ severity). <b>Rain</b> ramp: dark green (light) &rarr; green &rarr; yellow &rarr; orange &rarr; red &rarr; magenta &rarr; purple (extreme). <b>Snow/Sleet</b> ramp: pale blue (light) &rarr; blue &rarr; purple (heavy). Same intensity sits at the same position on both ramps. Type is observed/analysed, never inferred from color: MRMS PrecipFlag (snow class 3) inside CONUS and the regional AK/HI/CARIB domains, ECCC SfcPrecipType (snow classes) in Canada, and GFS CSNOW/CICEP for model snow/ice in verified radar gaps only. Echoes from sources that publish no type (OPERA EU, JMA) stay on the Rain ramp. No echo = transparent; GFS pixels are model estimates, never radar. GFS model estimates (not radar) use the same two ramps where no radar covers.</p><p>This entry auto-refreshes from the live overlay (source: NOAA/NSSL MRMS SeamlessHSR hybrid-scan reflectivity composite (CONUS, Alaska, Hawaii, Caribbean; dBZ, public domain) + ECCC North American Radar Composite 1km rain (RADAR_1KM_RRAI, mm/h) / snow (RADAR_1KM_RSNO, cm/h) / precipitation type (Radar_1km_SfcPrecipType) + EUMETNET OPERA EU DBZH composite (CC BY 4.0) in remaining radar gaps + JMA Japan nowcast (attribution) in Japan gaps + NOAA GFS model estimates, same colors (public domain) in verified radar gaps only).</p><p>Turn on/off independently of all other layers. Add this file once; new source cycles appear automatically.</p><p><i>Not endorsed by NOAA.</i></p>]]></description>
      <Link>
        <href>https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/kml/live/North_America_Live_Precipitation.kml</href>
        <refreshMode>onInterval</refreshMode>
        <refreshInterval>300</refreshInterval>
      </Link>
    </NetworkLink>
  </Document>
</kml>
